Subject: [PATCH] Phase 04: Agent modes and personalities (six named
 identities)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds modes.py: six named agent personalities that share one runtime but
each bring a focused system-prompt prefix, a default tool whitelist, and
tailored step/stall limits. The active mode is stored in SQLite as a
project-scoped 'decision' memory entry so it persists across restarts and
appears in the project's decision history.

The six modes
  researcher   — read-only by default; structured findings, explicit
                 uncertainty; restricted tool set (no write/run tools)
  planner      — writes an ordered plan to memory before acting; prefers
                 small reversible changes; full tool access
  coding_agent — the existing default workhorse; full tool access;
                 apply_change_with_test for all edits (unchanged behaviour)
  mini_divs    — Divs' over-engineering alter ego; questions requirements,
                 proposes architecture first, opinionated; full tools;
                 higher step budget (30) for bigger tasks
  intern       — cautious, fully transparent; explains every action before
                 running it; stops and asks on ambiguity
  growth       — writing/content/research only; never touches code or
                 runs commands; restricted tool set

New module:
  modes.py
    - Mode dataclass: id, display_name, description,
      system_prompt_prefix, allowed_tools (None=all), default_max_steps,
      default_max_stalls.
    - MODES dict of all six; DEFAULT_MODE_ID = "coding_agent".
    - set_active_mode(project_id, mode_id, db_path) — stores as a
      'decision' memory entry, superseding any previous mode entry
      (upsert semantics via memory.supersede, not duplicate rows).
    - get_active_mode(project_id, db_path) — reads back the active entry;
      falls back to coding_agent if none set.
    - list_modes() — summary of all six for display.

  test_modes.py — 22 tests across 4 classes:
    TestModeRegistry (8), TestActiveModeStorage (7),
    TestModeAwareRunTask (4), TestModeForgeTools (3).

Changes to forge.py:
  - `import modes as _modes` added.
  - run_task() signature: max_steps/max_stalls now default to None
    (resolved from active mode; caller-supplied values still override).
  - Mode-aware system message: active_mode.system_prompt_prefix is
    prepended to _SYSTEM_MESSAGE["content"] with a --- separator before
    each run, so the LLM knows its current role without touching the
    shared tool-docs block.
  - Two new tool functions: set_mode_tool, list_modes_tool.
  - Two new ToolSpec entries (risks: write / read).
  - System prompt extended with docs + JSON examples for set_mode and
    list_modes tools.

Backward compatibility: a project with no stored mode runs exactly as
before — coding_agent defaults, full tool access, no prompt change.
All 149 tests pass (127 prior + 22 new); no stray .db files produced.

